# Squares with three loaded edges: the fifteen-face run `L31a`

Generated by `ai_research_notes/outerplanar/t4b_m4/gen15.py runs`. For each run of
`ai_research_notes/OUTERPLANAR_13_15_LEAN_PLAN.md` §2.3 (the square lemmas of the fifteen-face note
`ai_research_notes/OUTERPLANAR_FIFTEEN_EVEN_2026-11-25.md`, certified in
`ai_research_notes/outerplanar/fivemarks/results.md`): the property of the 52 patterns of the cover,
from the records of `Outerplanar/Sq15Data/`, the list-level theorem, and its reflection (the same
square read from the other end of the root edge). In each, `W j` is the profile of the path edge
`j` of a square `u x₀ x₁ v` (lists `Lu`, `Li 0`, `Li 1`, `Lv`), and `N j` its scale.

The certificates are exact (kernel-checked integer Gibbs inequalities, no logarithms); they
replace the float-oracle certificates of `fivemarks/fm_solve.py` and `fm_solve2.py`, re-solved in
this format on the 52 saturated patterns instead of the 4202 list configurations.
-/

